{"title":"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we make five two-digit numbers using the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b5f62f6e30626204b7ed9939dd5b49ca146573.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 1, 2, \\ldots 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> exactly once, and the product of the five numbers is maximized, find the greatest number among them. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greedy_algorithm\" title=\"Greedy algorithm\">greedy algorithm</a> question. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06917268b64462d53504965f84ebbf7699d6c5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}, b_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> be the digits of the first number, etc. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\">Without loss of generality</a> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/276281a6566c70a760de924412450b3cdf07854c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a_1 + b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" /> be the greatest number. Then we want to maximize the quantity\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259ba4da318d0946ebad3341579c468b0e3d3287.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(10a_1 + b_1)(10a_2 + b_2) \\cdots (10a_5 + b_5)\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c4008a58fae521f1e602a73300b16fc45df15071.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=10^5 a_1a_2a_3a_4a_5 + 10^4(b_1a_2a_3a_4a_5 + \\ldots) + \\ldots + b_1b_2b_3b_4b_5\\]\" width=\"458\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>The greedy algorithm quickly tells us that the first digits of the numbers should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/3/123b2fb4f8a0ff558d3f0f24711c3c0144c4d5ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9,8,7,6,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc7c33f5a690d839b4e8b4941ad3a2df8786f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />. Now, look at the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed99f78014bdf57b62e04864d28c977b06fb23ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />. The product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/6/876b4626316c9c50a8dd844e8fc34e0f31c7dd64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2a_3a_4a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"10\" /> is less than any of the other terms (which all contain the maximal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/c/cdc7c33f5a690d839b4e8b4941ad3a2df8786f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />), so by the greedy algorithm, we should make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> as small as possible. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/f/32f25f30e2bf419190d9774c0dd676b8d91f4b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC\" title=\"1997 PMWC\">1997 PMWC </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I13\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I13\">Problem I13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I15\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I15\">Problem I15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">I: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I1\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I2\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I3\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I4\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I5\" title=\"1997 PMWC Problems/Problem I5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wi